PhotoCraft is an open-source, native image editor written in Rust that works
the way Photoshop users expect: layers, masks, adjustment layers, layer
styles, type, vectors, brushes and selections, with 8/16/32-bit documents
and layered PSD/PSB files that round-trip. The canvas is composited on the
GPU through wgpu, with a CPU compositor as the reference.

The package also installs photocraft-cli, a headless converter and command
runner for batch work and automation.
